; THE JAVASCRIPT DOUBLE-INCREMENT (loopshape-2026-08-25 §3).
; expect: 0 1 2 3 4 4 4 4 4
;
; A loop whose counter is updated identically by every `again` has that update
; hoisted into the host `for` statement's post clause. The first version patched
; each backend's emitAgain separately; JavaScript's routes through the shared
; changedArgs instead, so the increment was emitted BOTH in the post clause and
; in the body and the counter advanced by two.
;
; It compiled. It ran. It returned a number. Only the ANSWER was wrong, which is
; what this suite exists to notice.
;
; Two clauses that both advance `i`, so the hoist fires; one that does not
; change `acc`, so the shapes differ per clause.
(def run (fn (n)
  (loop ((acc 0) (i 0))
    (@ge i n)   acc
    (@gt i 3)   (again acc (@add i 1))
    else        (again (@add acc 1) (@add i 1)))))
